E.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "service_role has BYPASSRLS, so RLS alone can't protect SECURITY DEFINER-only tables; permanent append-only tables (credit_ledger, audit_events) revoke insert/update/delete from all roles including service_role, proven by SQLSTATE 42501 negative tests."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_rule_12_fail_visibly", "label": "Rule 12: Fail visibly, not silently", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never report success when something was bypassed or a state change left no visible trace \u2014 applied both to DB writes and to UI state (e.g. a cleared search box that silently keeps filtering)."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_rule_14_investigate_before_escalate", "label": "Rule 14: Investigate before you escalate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When a bug/flag surfaces, dispatch an agent to establish validity, full extent, and a proposed fix before presenting the case \u2014 a fix scoped only to the reported symptom leaves siblings broken."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_control_one_layer_above_pattern", "label": "'Control one layer above the write happens' pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recurring bug class: a producer and consumer of a gated value (e.g. emailConfirmed, is_primary) drift out of lockstep because the consumer assumes a state the producer never actually guarantees; fix is to move the check to the shared producer, not each caller."}, {"id": "concept_f1_f5_cpd_rel